    "description": "Before-save flow that stamps Benchmark Last Reviewed whenever Tracking Benchmark is edited.\n\n=== IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS ===\n\n* Record-triggered before-save (fast field update) flow on Account. Entry: record is updated AND Tracking Benchmark IsChanged -> set the date.\n\n* Kobi reviewed it live and approved: 'Tracking benchmark is changed. Every time a record is updated and tracking benchmark is changed. We're going to set the date. Yeah, this is fine. This look good.'\n\n* NAMING CONVENTION: \\[Account\\] Before Save – Set Benchmark Last Reviewed. Per Kobi: 'we label it so that it has the object, whether it's a before save flow after save flow, and then the description.' Fast field updates are before-save; actions and related records are after-save. Screen flows get 'Screen' in front.\n\n* Field must stay manually editable despite being auto-set.\n\n=== ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA ===\n\n* Editing Tracking Benchmark updates the date; editing any other field does not.\n\n=== NOTES ===\n\n* ALREADY BUILT. Taryn built it before the Aug 17 call and Kobi approved it live. It is the only flow she has built so far — 'No, that was the only one I created.' Add the actual flow API name to the card.\n\n* Accepted limitation, confirmed with Joyce on Aug 13: if the benchmark is reviewed and the value doesn't change, the date goes stale unless someone edits it manually. Joyce: 'That's fine.'\n\n* The requirement flipped: Taryn relayed that the client wanted it automated; Kobi had it as manual — 'Automated. Okay... I don't remember.' Resolved in the client's favour.\n\n=== SOURCE ===\n\n* Aug 13 call — Joyce confirmed auto-stamp\n\n* Slack Taryn Aug 14 — built\n\n* Aug 17 call — reviewed and approved live\n\nDependencies: BUILD-127\n\nOwner (proposed): Taryn Reithofer\n\nRemember to update the requirements documentation as part of this change.\n\nCreated 2026-08-17 from the Operator/Partner ticket review, approved by Kobi.",
